AB  - Objective: To observe the impacts of electroacupuncture (EA) stimulation at "Zusanli and Kunlun Points" on spinal dorsal horn microglia activation in L5 spinal nerve ligation (SNL) rats and BNDF, P2 x 4 and GABAA gamma 2, and the changes in spinal dorsal horn synaptic plasticity in model rats.
   Methods: Adult male SD rats (180-220 g) were selected and randomly divided into 6 groups, including the sham group, the SNL group, the SNL + EA group, the SNL+5-BDBD group, the SNL + EA + 5-BDBD group and the SNL + FEA group. The changes in the Iba-1, BDNF, P2 x 4 and GABAA gamma 2 in the spinal cord of rats were observed by Western blotting, immunofluorescence, RT-PCR and other techniques; the long-term changes in the potential after the excitatory synapse of the spinal dorsal horn in rats were observed by in vivo electrophysiological technique.
   Results: After 7 days of intervention, the fluorescence intensity (FI) of P2 x 4 and Iba-1 in the SNL + EA group was lower than that in the SNL group and higher than that in the sham group(P < 0.01), but the FI of GABA(A)gamma 2 was higher than that in the SNL group(P < 0.01); the expression of Iba-1, BDNF and P2 x 4 proteins in the SNL + EA group, the SNL+5-BDBD group and the SNL + EA + 5-BDBD group was significantly lower than that in the SNL + FEA group(P < 0.05), but the expression of GABAA gamma 2 protein was higher (P < 0.05); after treatment with EA, the expression levels of Iba-1 mRNA and P2 x 4 mRNA in the SNL + EA group were lower than those in the SNL group(P < 0.01), but the expression levels of GABAA gamma 2 mRNA were higher (P < 0.01). Meanwhile, long-term potentiation changes could not be induced in the SNL + EA group.
   Conclusion: The EA stimulation at "Zusanli" and "Kunlun" points can improve the pain threshold of rats with neuropathic pain (NP), inhibit the excitatory postsynaptic potential (EPSP), and weaken the excitatory transmission efficiency between synapses during NP.
