AB  - The neurosteroid allopregnanolone has potent analgesic effects, and its potential use for neuropathic pain is supported by recent reports. However, the analgesic mechanisms are obscure. The voltage-gated sodium channels (Na-v) alpha subunit Na(v)1.3 is thought to play an essential role in neuropathic pain. Here, we report the effects of allopregnanolone sulfate (APAS) on sodium currents (I-Na) in Xenopus oocytes expressing Na(v)1.3 with beta(1) and beta(3 )subunits. APAS suppressed I-Na of Na(v)1.3 with beta(1) and beta(3) in a concentration-dependent manner (IC50 values; 75 and 26 mu mol/L). These results suggest the possible importance of Na(v)1.3 inhibition for the analgesic mechanisms of allopregnanolone. (C) 2018 The Authors. Production and hosting by Elsevier B.V. on behalf of Japanese Pharmacological Society.
