AB  - Some P2X3 receptor antagonists have been developed as new therapeutic drugs for pain. We discovered a novel chemotype of P2X3 receptor antagonists with a pyrrolinone skeleton. Because of SAR studies to improve bioavailability of lead compound 2, compound (R)-24 was identified, which showed an analgesic effect against neuropathic pain by oral administration. We constructed a human P2X3 homology model as a template for the zebrafish P2X4 receptor, which agreed with SAR studies of pyrrolinone derivatives.
